// # c_emit Fix — sum String+unit lower and match exhaustiveness check
//
// Logline: Lower a `Result[Option[X], Y]` (or user sum `pub type Foo = A(String) | B;`) into a tag-based OoRes_OptionX struct instead of fail-closing at ooda/oodac/c_emit_result_ty.oo:87, and gate ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_stmt.oo and ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo on ooda/oodac/tc_match_exh.oo:typecheck_match_exhaustive so a missing Ok/Err or sum arm is caught at emit-c, not just at `oodac check`.
//
// Setup: 1405 BLOCKED rows in openOODA/audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot; 29 in the `exit0` cat (audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot:75-80) trace to `ERR c_emit Result[Option/Result] residual` at c_emit_result_ty.oo:87; 7 in the same cat (audit/library_status_support_2.oot:6,9,52,111,113,193,195) trace to `ERR c_emit match-let expected Err or None` at c_emit_match_let.oo:190. Lane: ooda/oodac/c_emit_*.oo + ooda/oodac/tc_match_exh.oo (compiler agent owns). No std/ rewrites. No public-site text edit. Pin: v0.204.0-beta. ROADMAP.oot row §5 honesty — sum String+unit and match exhaust — both currently closed by public-site text; this spec turns them into real C locks.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Goal + non-Goals.
//   2. Two concrete current-pain row sets (3 rows per item, file:line).
//   3. Root cause: 2 families (sum C shape, match exhaust gate).
//   4. Proposed fix: 2 file edits with before/after diffs.
//   5. Acceptance criteria: 12 BLOCKED rows move GREEN, exhaust check fires at emit-c.
//   6. Risks: nested match, wildcard `_`, depth tracking.

// ## 1. Goal
//
// (a) `Result[Option[X], Y]` and the user-sum `pub type Foo = A(String) | B;` lower to a real C struct (`OoRes_OptionX` or `Foo`) and match. The driver exits 0 and gcc accepts. Today both fail-close: c_emit_result_ty.oo:87 prints `ERR\tc_emit\tResult[Option|Result] residual` then process_exit(1); the user-sum path in c_emit_sum.oo:91 emits the right struct shape, but c_emit_match_let.oo:42-48 only routes there when arm1 is a known ctor, so an unknown-shape sum leaks to the Ok/Err fast path and aborts at c_emit_match_let.oo:190.
//
// (b) A `match` on a Result, Option, or user sum that drops a variant fails at `emit-c`, not only at `oodac check`. Today typecheck_match_exhaustive lives at ooda/oodac/tc_match_exh.oo:127 and is called only from ooda/oodac/check_drive.oo:144; ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_stmt.oo:63 and ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo:19 never call it, so a `match r { Ok(x) => x }` (no Err) emits `if (__m.ok) { ... }` with no else branch and gcc silently produces an uninit `__m.val` on the missing path.
//
// Non-goals:
//   - No new type lattice; reuse the 11 ctor kinds in ooda/oodac/ty.oo:20-30 (I, S, U).
//   - No std/ rewrites; all 6 affected std files (cloud, database, sec/crypto, sec/sys, sec/watermark) keep their types as-is.
//   - No change to ROADMAP public-site text; this spec moves the §5 rows from "site-closed" to "code-closed".
//   - No edits to ooda/oodac/ty.oo (data-only per Phase A rule, audit/green/c_emit_refactor_phase_a.oot:84); c_emit_*.oo is the lane.

// ## 2. Current pain (6 concrete rows, 3 per item)
//
// ### Item 1 — sum String+unit (Result[Option[X], Y])
//
// | # | audit file:line | std file | std file:line (type decl) | error | shape wanted |
// |---|-----------------|----------|---------------------------|-------|--------------|
// | 1 | openOODA/audit/library_status_tail_3.oot:108 | ooda/std/cloud/cloud.oo | (facade; etcd_client) | `ERR c_emit Result[Option/Result] residual` at c_emit_result_ty.oo:87 | `OoRes_OptionEtcdKeyValue { int ok; long long v0; OoStr s0; }` |
// | 2 | openOODA/audit/library_status_tail_3.oot:110 | ooda/std/cloud/etcd_client.oo | ooda/std/cloud/etcd_client.oo:120 (fn return `Result[Option[EtcdKeyValue], String]`) | same | same |
// | 3 | openOODA/audit/library_status_tail_4.oot:218 | ooda/std/database/database.oo | (facade; lsm_sstable, lsm_tree) | same | `OoRes_OptionString { int ok; long long v0; OoStr s0; }` |
// | 4 | openOODA/audit/library_status_tail_4.oot:223 | ooda/std/database/lsm_sstable.oo | ooda/std/database/lsm_sstable.oo:140 (fn return `Result[Option[String], String]`) | same | same |
// | 5 | openOODA/audit/library_status_tail_4.oot:224 | ooda/std/database/lsm_tree.oo | ooda/std/database/lsm_tree.oo:165 (fn return `Result[Option[String], String]`) | same | same |
// | 6 | openOODA/audit/library_status_tail_3.oot:111 | ooda/std/cloud/etcd_watch.oo | (uses etcd_client_get return; same shape) | same | same |
//
// All 6 are `exit0` category in audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot:23,75-80. The inner Option is the unit-or-String shape: Some(X) -> long long v0 + ok=1; None -> OoStr s0="" + ok=0. The Ok side has a payload (long long when X is Int/Bool, OoStr when X is String), the Err side is a plain String error.
//
// ### Item 2 — match exhaustiveness (c_emit silent on missing arm)
//
// | # | audit file:line | std file | std file:line (match) | error | arm dropped |
// |---|-----------------|----------|------------------------|-------|-------------|
// | 1 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_2.oot:6 | ooda/std/sec/crypto/poly1305.oo | (re-export facade; nested through poly1305_stubs.oo:110 `match mac_res { Ok(expected_tag) => { ... }, Err(e) => ... }`) | `ERR c_emit match-let expected Err or None` at c_emit_match_let.oo:190 | arm misread: c_emit_block returns after the inner `if { return Err(...) }` RBRACE, then the outer block sees `true` not `Err` |
// | 2 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_2.oot:9 | ooda/std/sec/crypto/poly1305_stubs.oo | ooda/std/sec/crypto/poly1305_stubs.oo:110,156,160,172 (4 match sites) | same | one match per facade-imported site; c_emit walks past the inner block's first RBRACE |
// | 3 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_2.oot:52 | ooda/std/sec/crypto/zksnark_stubs.oo | (transitive; uses poly1305_stubs pattern) | same | same pattern (nested match in Ok arm) |
// | 4 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_2.oot:111 | ooda/std/sec/sys/cfi_engine.oo | ooda/std/sec/sys/cfi_engine.oo:92 `let site_matched: Bool = match site_res { Ok(site) => { if ... { ... } true }, Err(e) => false }` | same | arm misread at the `if` body's closing RBRACE |
// | 5 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_2.oot:113 | ooda/std/sec/sys/cfi_stubs.oo | (transitive; same cfi_engine pattern) | same | same |
// | 6 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_2.oot:193 | ooda/std/sec/watermark.oo | (facade; transitive match) | same | same |
// | 7 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_2.oot:195 | ooda/std/sec/watermark_engine.oo | (transitive; same pattern) | same | same |
//
// All 7 are `exit0` category (audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot:23,75-80). The audit's `declarations` and `other` cats also have match-driven rows but they are gcc-side (`expected expression before '[' token`) and out of this spec's lane.

// ## 3. Root cause
//
// ### 3.1 Sum String+unit — c_emit_result_ty.oo:86-90 fail-closes
//
// The 11-ctor kind table in ooda/oodac/ty.oo:20-30 covers Int/Float/Bool/Str/Unit/List/Result/Name/Cap/Ref/RefMut. The kind `Option[X]` is not a ctor — Option is a soft alias for `Result[X, unit]` (openOODA/audit/green/c_emit_refactor_phase_a.oot §2 floor). The c_emit path at ooda/oodac/c_emit_result_ty.oo:12-91 picks an OoResX kind by reading the IDENT after `Result[`. For `Result[Option[X], Y]` the IDENT is `Option`, which is not in the switch (lines 31-85), so it falls through to the `Option/Result` branch at line 86-90 and aborts. The fall-through was a deliberate fail-closed (openOODA/audit/green/fix_slist_oob_sem_recovery.oot:25 keeps it as residual), but with ty.oo now landable the same shape can be lowered to `OoRes_OptionX` using the same `(int ok, long long v0, OoStr s0)` slot triple the sum spec already emits at ooda/oodac/c_emit_sum.oo:91.
//
// ### 3.2 Match exhaust — c_emit_match_let.oo:184-192 aborts, typecheck never runs
//
// ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo:155-161 picks BLOCK vs EXPR for the Ok arm body. For the BLOCK path (LBRACE), it calls ooda/oodac/c_emit_helpers.oo:12-47 c_emit_block. c_emit_block walks while-loop with no LBRACE/RBRACE depth counter (lines 21-42); it calls c_emit_stmt for each statement, which dispatches to c_emit_if_stmt at c_emit_stmt.oo:151-183 for KW_IF. c_emit_if_stmt at line 160 calls c_emit_block for the if body, which closes at the if's matching RBRACE. c_emit_block then sees the next statement; in poly1305_stubs.oo:110-129 and cfi_engine.oo:92-118 the next statement is `true` or another stmt, and the OUTER block's closing RBRACE is one token later. c_emit_block then breaks correctly. So in theory this should work. The actual cause is ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo:167-170: after the BLOCK path, control falls into c_emit_expr_c (the EXPR path) which RE-PARSES the Ok arm body. c_emit_expr_c → c_emit_expr_prec → c_emit_primary_c (ooda/oodac/c_emit_ops.oo:106-144) walks one expression and stops — but the first primary in the Ok arm block is a LBRACE (the arm's `{`), and c_emit_primary_c does not consume the LBRACE block body; it stops at LBRACE and returns. p is now still pointing at the Ok arm's opening LBRACE. Then c_match_skip_comma at ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo:183 (used by both arms in fallback) reads `c_tokt(toks, p)` which returns `Ok` (the arm1 name), so arm2 check at line 189-191 sees `Ok != Err/None` and aborts.
//
// Separately, ooda/oodac/tc_match_exh.oo:127 typecheck_match_exhaustive exists and is correct for `let x: T = Some(1); match x { ... }` (line 134-176 find the annotation; line 223-235 fire for Option/Result/user-sum), but ooda/oodac/check_drive.oo:144 is the only caller. c_emit_match_stmt.oo:63 and c_emit_match_let.oo:19 never call it, so `emit-c` on a non-exhaustive match produces a half-emitted C file (no else branch) and gcc sees an uninit `__m.val` warning, not a real error.

// ## 4. Proposed fix
//
// Two files touched. No std/ rewrites. No edits to ooda/oodac/ty.oo. Lane: ooda/oodac/c_emit_result_ty.oo + ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo (both already in the compiler agent's lane per audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot:46, 53, 91, 92).
//
// ### 4.1 Lower `Result[Option[X], Y]` to `OoRes_OptionX`
//
// File: ooda/oodac/c_emit_result_ty.oo. Replace the fail-close at line 86-90 with a real lower. Use the same tag/slot pattern as ooda/oodac/c_emit_sum.oo:91 so the existing match path in c_emit_match_let.oo:42-44 (which already routes user sums to c_emit_sum_match_let) just works for `Option[X]` once the ctor name is `__opt_some` / `__opt_none`.
//
// BEFORE (ooda/oodac/c_emit_result_ty.oo:86-90):
// ```c
//     if e == "Option" || e == "Result" {
//         println("ERR\tc_emit\tResult[Option|Result] residual");
//         process_exit(1);
//         return "";
//     }
//     return "OoRes_" + e;
// ```
//
// AFTER (insert at the same site, change the return to a real typedef):
// ```c
//     if e == "Option" {
//         // Result[Option[X], Y] -> OoRes_OptionX with (int ok, long long v0, OoStr s0).
//         // Reuse the c_emit_sum slot triple (c_emit_sum.oo:91) so c_emit_match_let.oo:42-44
//         // and c_emit_sum_match_let (c_emit_sum.oo:134-214) handle Some/None via __ml.tag.
//         let mut ep: Int = p + 1;
//         if ep < n && c_tokk(toks, ep) == "LBRACKET" {
//             let inner: String = c_emit_peek_inner_ident(toks, ep, n);
//             let slot: String = "OoRes_Option" + inner;
//             c_emit_sum_alias_for(slot, "int ok; long long v0; OoStr s0;");
//             return slot;
//         }
//         return "OoRes_Option";
//     }
//     if e == "Result" {
//         // Result[Result[X, _], Y] stays fail-closed (only Option is a soft alias; Result-of-Result is a true sum that needs the user sum path).
//         println("ERR\tc_emit\tResult[Result[...]] residual");
//         process_exit(1);
//         return "";
//     }
//     return "OoRes_" + e;
// ```
//
// Helper additions (one new tiny file `ooda/oodac/c_emit_opt_ty.oo`, ≤ 40 lines): `c_emit_peek_inner_ident` reads the IDENT after `LBRACKET` of `Option[...]`; `c_emit_sum_alias_for` is a 4-line shim around ooda/oodac/c_emit_sum.oo:87-100 c_try_emit_sum_alias that takes a custom slot triple string. The `Some(x)` / `None` ctor site already emits `__ctor__Some` and `__ctor__None` via c_emit_sum.oo:42-66 (when the user wrote `pub type Opt = Some(X) | None;`); for the new path, register the ctors at the call site of c_result_c_ty by adding two `c_env_put` lines: `e = c_env_put(e, "__ctor__Some", "OoRes_OptionX:0:I"); e = c_env_put(e, "__ctor__None", "OoRes_OptionX:1:U");` where X is the inner type IDENT. With ctors registered, c_emit_match_let.oo:42-44 routes to c_emit_sum_match_let, which already binds v0 (Some) and emits no payload (None) at ooda/oodac/c_emit_sum.oo:193-197.
//
// ### 4.2 Gate c_emit on typecheck_match_exhaustive and fix the EXPR path
//
// File: ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo. Two changes:
//
// (a) At line 32 (after `let rkind: String = c_match_rkind(e, scrut);`) call the typecheck so a non-exhaustive match fails at emit-c. Import at top of file: `import "tc_match_exh.oo";`. Then add `typecheck_match_exhaustive(toks);` (ooda/oodac/tc_match_exh.oo:127) — it walks the whole token stream and is idempotent; cheap enough to call once per match.
//
// BEFORE (ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo:32-33):
// ```c
//     let rkind: String = c_match_rkind(e, scrut);
//     if p >= n || c_tokk(toks, p) != "LBRACE" {
// ```
//
// AFTER:
// ```c
//     let rkind: String = c_match_rkind(e, scrut);
//     typecheck_match_exhaustive(toks);
//     if p >= n || c_tokk(toks, p) != "LBRACE" {
// ```
//
// Same one-line call added at ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_stmt.oo:98 (just after `let rkind: String = c_match_rkind(env, scrut);`).
//
// (b) Remove the re-parse at line 167-170 (the EXPR path) for the BLOCK case so c_emit_block is the only path. The current code runs BOTH the BLOCK branch (line 155-161) and the EXPR branch (line 167-170) back-to-back when arm1 is followed by LBRACE — the EXPR branch's c_emit_expr_c returns with p still at the Ok arm's opening LBRACE, so the next arm2 check at line 189 sees `Ok` again.
//
// BEFORE (ooda/oodac/c_emit_match_let.oo:155-170):
// ```c
//     if p < n && c_tokk(toks, p) == "LBRACE" {
//         let br: List[String] = c_emit_block(toks, p, n, eok);
//         p = parse_int(list_get(br, 0));
//     } else {
//         let st: List[String] = c_emit_stmt(toks, p, n, eok);
//         p = parse_int(list_get(st, 0));
//     }
//     oo_emit_tmp_leave();
//     p = c_match_skip_comma(toks, p, n);
//     println("  } else {");
//     // Err arm
//     if p >= n || c_tokk(toks, p) != "IDENT" {
//         println("ERR\tc_emit\tmatch-let expected Err or None");
//         process_exit(1);
//     }
// ```
//
// AFTER:
// ```c
//     if p < n && c_tokk(toks, p) == "LBRACE" {
//         let br: List[String] = c_emit_block(toks, p, n, eok);
//         p = parse_int(list_get(br, 0));
//     } else {
//         let pr_ok: List[String] = c_emit_expr_c(toks, p, n, eok);
//         p = parse_int(list_get(pr_ok, 0));
//         let mut okx = list_get(pr_ok, 1);
//         oo_emit_tmp_own(okx);
//         if c_env_get(e, "__ret_int__") == "1" {
//             if !is_some {
//                 if rkind != "RI" { okx = "oo_str_to_int(" + okx + ")"; }
//             }
//         }
//         if decl == 0 { c_emit_reassign_arc(name, okx, eok); } else { println("    " + name + " = " + okx + ";"); }
//     }
//     oo_emit_tmp_leave();
//     p = c_match_skip_comma(toks, p, n);
//     println("  } else {");
//     // Err arm
//     if p >= n || c_tokk(toks, p) != "IDENT" {
//         println("ERR\tc_emit\tmatch-let expected Err or None");
//         process_exit(1);
//     }
// ```
//
// The AFTER block moves the EXPR-only logic (lines 167-178 in the current file) INSIDE the `else` branch of the LBRACE test, so BLOCK arms use c_emit_block and don't get re-parsed. Same fix mirrored in c_emit_match_stmt.oo:155-161 (the BLOCK/EXPR dispatch).
//
// ### 4.3 Bonus — register ctors for `Result[Option[X], Y]`
//
// In ooda/oodac/c_emit_result.oo:c_lower_ok_err (line 50-139), add a branch so that when `__ret__` is the new `RO` kind (Result[Option[X], Y]) and the call is `Some(v)`, emit the tag-based tuple: `((OoRes_OptionX){0, 0, oo_str_lit("")})` for None and `((OoRes_OptionX){1, v, oo_str_lit("")})` for Some(v) where v is a `long long` (Int) or `OoStr` (String) per ty.oo:20-30. This replaces the missing fall-through path; the 4th ACCEPT in §5 needs this so c_emit can build the call's return value, not just the match.
//
// Lane check: ooda/oodac/c_emit_result.oo is compiler-agent lane (audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot:91). ooda/oodac/c_emit_result_ty.oo and c_emit_match_let.oo are the same lane (audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot:46, 53, 75-80, 91).

// ## 5. Acceptance criteria
//
// | # | gate | measure | target |
// |---|------|---------|--------|
// | 1 | Item 1 rows GREEN | BLOCKED -> GREEN count for the 6 audit file:line rows in §2 item 1 (cloud, database facets) | 6 rows |
// | 2 | Result[Option[String], String] smoke | `ooda/scripts/result_opt_str_smoke.oo` (new, ≤ 30 lines) emit-c + gcc -O2 + run prints `result_opt_str: PASSED` | new lock |
// | 3 | user sum String+unit smoke | new fixture `ooda/fixtures/sum_string_unit.oo` (≤ 30 lines: `pub type Foo = A(String) | B; pub fn make(s: String) -> Foo { if s == "" { return B; } return A(s); } pub fn main() { let x = make("hi"); let y = match x { A(s) => s, B => "empty" }; println(y); }`) emit-c + gcc + run prints `hi` | new lock |
// | 4 | item 2 exhaust check at emit-c | BLOCKED -> GREEN for the 7 audit file:line rows in §2 item 2 (sec/crypto, sec/sys, sec/watermark) | 7 rows |
// | 5 | typecheck fires at emit-c | `ooda/scripts/exhaust_emit_smoke.oo` (new, ≤ 30 lines) runs `oodac emit-c fixtures/open_match_option_bad.oo` and asserts non-zero exit + stderr contains `non-exhaustive` | new lock |
// | 6 | `_` wildcard accepted | `ooda/scripts/wildcard_smoke.oo` (new, ≤ 25 lines) runs `oodac emit-c fixtures/exhaust_wildcard.oo` (new fixture, ≤ 15 lines: `pub fn main() { let x: Result[String, String] = Ok(""); let y = match x { _ => 0 }; println(y); }`) and asserts exit 0 | new lock |
// | 7 | nested match arm find | `ooda/scripts/nested_match_smoke.oo` (new, ≤ 30 lines) runs `oodac emit-c fixtures/nested_match_arm.oo` (new fixture with inner `if { return Err(...) }` block in Ok arm, mirrors cfi_engine.oo:92) and asserts exit 0 + gcc -O2 | new lock |
// | 8 | master catalog delta | `openOODA/audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot` `exit0` category drops from 29 to 16 (13 rows: 6 from §2.1 + 7 from §2.2) | measurable |
// | 9 | no new BLOCKED | sum of `redef` + `missing_type` + `dot_arrow` + `declarations` cats does not increase after the fix runs against the full std batch | ≤ current 1405 - 13 = 1392 |
// | 10 | lane discipline | no edit to ooda/oodac/ty.oo (data-only per audit/green/c_emit_refactor_phase_a.oot:84); no edit to ooda/oodac/c_emit_sum.oo (already correct shape) | grep `-c "ty.oo" fix_sum_exhaust.oot` = 0 for edits, ≥ 2 for cite |
// | 11 | line count | this file ≤ 256 lines; new c_emit_opt_ty.oo ≤ 40 lines; c_emit_match_let.oo ≤ 256 lines after edit | `wc -l` |
// | 12 | SHIPPED update | openOODA/SHIPPED.oot row "sum String+unit emit" moves to SHIPPED with cite to this spec and the new c_emit_opt_ty.oo | board edit |

// ## 6. Risks
//
// | risk | shape | mitigation |
// |------|-------|------------|
// | R1 nested match in match arm (match-let inside Ok arm) | c_emit_sum_match_let at ooda/oodac/c_emit_sum.oo:134-214 walks arms with a `__ml.tag` switch; nested match is not detected and the inner `__ml` shadows. Smoke fixture R7 above catches this; if it fails, the fix in §4.2(b) (single-pass BLOCK) prevents the outer arm walk from re-entering. |
// | R2 `_` wildcard semantics | ooda/oodac/tc_match_exh.oo:99-101 returns early on `_`, so any ctor list passes. c_emit_match_stmt.oo:79-82 and c_emit_match_let.oo:42-48 still require the Ok/Some IDENT first, so `match r { _ => x }` is not yet wired. R6 acceptance gate covers the wildcard-only fixture; if it fails, the fix is to add `_ => return;` fallthrough in c_emit_match_stmt.oo:117 (after the Ok arm) and c_emit_match_let.oo:153. |
// | R3 depth tracking in c_emit_block | ooda/oodac/c_emit_helpers.oo:12-47 c_emit_block does not track LBRACE/RBRACE depth itself; it relies on c_emit_stmt to consume nested blocks. The new fix relies on the same assumption. If a future change adds a stmt that does not fully consume its inner block, c_emit_block will break at the wrong RBRACE. Add a depth counter as defensive (line 21): `let mut depth: Int = 0; if k == "LBRACE" { depth = depth + 1; }` and only break on RBRACE when `depth == 0`. Out of scope for this spec; tracked as a follow-up. |
// | R4 Result[Result[X, Y], Z] is a real sum, not a soft alias | c_emit_result_ty.oo:86-90 keeps the fail-closed for `e == "Result"`. Documented in the AFTER block of §4.1. User must write a `pub type` for that case. |
